{"title":"Implicit differentiation","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Implicit differentiation</b> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">differentiating</a> both sides of an implicit <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> with respect to one of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Variable\" title=\"Variable\">variables</a>. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dependent_variable&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Dependent variable (page does not exist)\">dependent variable</a> is treated as a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Independent_variable&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Independent variable (page does not exist)\">independent variable</a> and is differentiated with the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chain_rule\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Chain rule\">chain rule</a>. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Formal_Definition\">Formal Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Implicit_differentiation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Formal Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Implicit_differentiation&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example\">Example</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Implicit_differentiation&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Example\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/500621cdf25e1e3a980d518b206e0e165ab203d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + xy^2 + x^2y + y^3 + sin(xy) = 2xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"291\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/15972aacfeb58207104beddc2176a5864ea566ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x^2 + (1y^2 + 2xy \\frac{dy}{dx}) + (2xy + x^2 \\frac{dy}{dx}) + 3y^2 \\frac{dy}{dx} + (cos(xy) (1y + 1x \\frac{dy}{dx}) = 2 (1y + 1x \\frac{dy}{dx})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"683\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d5b6fdee102469cd82da34c51b63eeaa998b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{dy}{dx} (2xy + x^2 + 3y^2 + xcos(xy) - 2x) = -3x^2 - y^2 - 2xy - ycos(xy) + 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"576\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/23554603e7e8f7f44903e9e91ed69b4896c6f482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{dy}{dx} = -\\frac{3x^2 + 2xy + y^2 + ycos(xy) - 2y}{x^2 + 2xy + 3y^2 + xcos(xy) - 2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"315\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Implicit_differentiation&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153904\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 35/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 513/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1045/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.571      1 -total\n 83.23%    5.469      2 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in